<title>OMAN: Oman awards $20 mln deal to Ericsson.</title>
<headline>Oman awards $20 mln deal to Ericsson.</headline>
<dateline>MUSCAT 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman has awarded a 7.7 million rials ($20 million) contract to Sweden's L.M. Ericsson to supply and operate new switching equipment for its GSM mobile telephone network.</p>
<p>&quot;The contract will add 50,000 lines to the current 38,000 line network to cope with increasing demand,&quot; Ahmed bin Suwaidan al-Balushi, Oman's Minister of Posts and Telecommunications told reporters on Monday.</p>
<p>Balushi said the new switching equipment will be operational in November.</p>
</text>
